religious iconography.", "document_ref": "d5", "source_ref": "s5", "qualifiers":
["topic: symbolic_interpretation"], "limitations": [], "confidence": "medium"},
    {"local_ref": "st20", "text": "The Aegis 18 volume provides a corpus of 
comparative Aegean images, including gold rings and wall paintings with sacred 
trees, altars, deities, and apotropaic motifs, which are used to contextualize 
