sepulchral treasure of gold signet-rings and bead-seals from Thisbe in Boeotia, 
and an interpretive section titled \"A glimpse into the Minoan after-world\". 
The work presents detailed descriptions and plates documenting the Ring of 
Nestor and associated objects, discusses their funerary context, and elaborates 
Evans's interpretation of the ring’s iconography as an expression of Minoan 
cultural and religious concepts, including afterlife beliefs.",
      "source_ref": "s4"
