re-evaluates the Ring of Nestor with a focus on its authenticity and 
iconography. It reports scientific analysis of the ring, including its gold 
composition with approximately 97% gold content, and compares the object with 
other Ancient Aegean goldwork. Vlachopoulos reviews earlier doubts about 
authenticity and uses metallurgical and stylistic evidence to address whether 
the ring is an ancient artefact, framing the discussion as part of a broader 
quest to assess the ring’s status.",
      "source_ref": "s5"
